---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.title}`}>
  <article class="reading">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="post-desc">Gear, money, and the everyday - from a family of four in the Bay Area.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Jason. I spent a decade in big tech - an engineer and data
        scientist at Google (on the spam and phishing detection side) and
        Facebook, then product at Twitter and Discord - with two early-stage
        startups acquired along the way. When we were expecting our first kid,
        I left to start a solo consulting LLC so I could do school dropoff and
        still do the work. That was five years ago. The business now supports
        our family - six figures a year, with the swings you'd expect from
        consulting - and this year it's growing past just me.
      </p>
      <p>
        We're in the Bay Area with a 4-year-old, an infant, and a 75-pound
        bernedoodle who's sure he's the third kid. pastelloclub is where that
        life runs into parenthood, written like what I used to do for a living:
        product teardowns and the numbers behind them. Three kinds of writing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Gear reviews written like teardowns - what held up after four years and
          two kids, what broke, and whether it earns its shelf space. Everything
          is rated on the Pastello Scale.
        </li>
        <li>
          Money math for parents who work for themselves - Trump Accounts, 529s,
          Solo 401(k)s, quarterly taxes. This isn't research; it's our accounts.
        </li>
        <li>
          Everyday notes - feeding small humans, surviving sleep regressions, the
          quiet ten minutes after they finally close their eyes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Everything here we bought ourselves and lived with, usually for years.
        And when I couldn't find a tool that did the job, I built it myself -
        Lullaby, a feeding-and-diaper tracker for our newborn, came out of
        exactly this stubbornness.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How this site makes money:</strong> affiliate links (Amazon,
        eBay) and occasional referral links - I run my LLC's bookkeeping,
        payroll, and taxes through{' '}
        <a href="https://share.collective.com/simplybootstrapped"
          >Collective</a
        >, and that's a referral link. It's also just what I use. The opinions
        aren't for sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        On privacy: I write about my kids but won't name them or show their
        faces, and money numbers get rounded to ranges I'm comfortable sharing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to say hello? Write us at
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
